# Line endings are a correctness matter here, not a style one.
#
# scripts/deploy archives the WORKING TREE, not git. On a Windows checkout with
# core.autocrlf=true and no rules, every shell script and every .rs file arrives
# CRLF — which would bake a `#!/bin/sh\r` entrypoint into the runner image (bad
# interpreter: every graded run fails) and ship student-facing sources with
# stray carriage returns.
#
# This bit the go-checkpoints repository on 2026-09-09 and was caught only
# because that deploy was moved to Linux; see go-checkpoints/docs/10-cloud-run.md
# §6. Nothing had protected this repository either.
#
# Anything the container executes, or that the toolchain reads, is pinned to LF.

* text=auto

*.sh        text eol=lf
*.rs        text eol=lf
*.toml      text eol=lf
*.js        text eol=lf
*.mjs       text eol=lf
*.cjs       text eol=lf
*.ts        text eol=lf
*.tsx       text eol=lf
*.json      text eol=lf
*.md        text eol=lf
*.sql       text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
*.html      text eol=lf
*.css       text eol=lf

Makefile    text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
*.template  text eol=lf
.env*       text eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gz  binary
